menu "WX101CH021I-40Z bring-up"
config SCREEN_ENABLE_DISPLAY
    bool "Enable the exact-model DSI color-bar trial"
    default n
    depends on IDF_TARGET_ESP32P4
    help
        Send the WX101CH021I-40Z 2-lane vendor initialization sequence
        and display a framebuffer color-bar pattern. Requires PSRAM.
        Backlight, hardware reset and touch control are not configured.
config SCREEN_ENABLE_BENCHMARK
    bool "Run the official LVGL 8 benchmark"
    default n
    depends on SCREEN_ENABLE_DISPLAY
    depends on !SCREEN_ENABLE_USB_DISPLAY
    help
        Use an RGB565 framebuffer and the P4 v3 bridge's RGB888 output
        conversion. Run the unmodified LVGL 8 benchmark at maximum speed.
config SCREEN_ENABLE_TOUCH_PROBE
    bool "Enable the JD9032 touch test and benchmark launcher"
    default n
    depends on SCREEN_ENABLE_BENCHMARK
    help
        Identify the controller at I2C address 0x68 and use the first finger
        as an LVGL pointer. The benchmark can be started with a touch button.
        No controller control registers or reset GPIOs are written.
config SCREEN_TOUCH_LATENCY_MARKER
    bool "Measure latency with the board RGB LED and camera"
    default n
    depends on SCREEN_ENABLE_TOUCH_PROBE
    help
        Use the board's GPIO51 WS2812 and a synchronous screen patch as
        an external camera timing reference. Temporary diagnostic mode.
config SCREEN_ENABLE_USB_DISPLAY
    bool "Receive USB High-Speed JPEG frames from the Mac extended display"
    default n
    depends on SCREEN_ENABLE_DISPLAY
    help
        HUSB carries a vendor bulk stream. Decode complete JPEG frames with
        the P4 hardware codec and hand off three packed BGR24 (RGB888)
        framebuffers.
endmenu
